@startuml state-ink-input
!include elvira.iuml
' What: how one pointer on a page becomes an annotation action. A pen always inks, a mouse inks, a finger inks only until a pen was seen (then fingers scroll); a second finger cancels the stroke so pinch zoom wins. The pen's eraser end erases whatever tool is picked.
' Kind: UML state diagram. Scope: useInkInput in one InkLayer.
' Source: src/composables/useInkInput.ts, src/stores/ink.ts (2026-11-18)

title Ink input: one pointer, from down to commit

[*] --> Idle

state Idle : touch after a pen was seen\nscrolls the page instead

state Inking <<focus>> {
  state Drawing : pen · highlighter · shape\nsamples from getCoalescedEvents()
  state Held : still for 600 ms\nsnaps to a line or shape
  [*] --> Drawing
  Drawing --> Held : no movement
  Held --> Drawing : pointermove
}

state Erasing : objects under the path are removed

state Editing {
  state Moving : selection follows the pointer
  state Resizing : scales from the opposite corner
  state Marquee : selects what it touches
}

Idle --> Inking : pointerdown\n[draw tool]
Idle --> Erasing : pointerdown\n[eraser, or pen eraser end]
Idle --> Moving : on an object\n[select tool]
Idle --> Resizing : on a handle
Idle --> Marquee : on empty page\n[select tool]

Inking --> Idle : pointerup / commit
Inking --> Idle : second finger, pointercancel / discard
Erasing --> Idle : pointerup / commit
Editing --> Idle : pointerup / commit

note bottom of Editing
  commit = one undo step
  and one save of the page
end note

caption Every gesture is one undo step and one save of its page, never a save per pointer sample.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersViewer · docs/diagrams/state-ink-input.puml
@enduml
